    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0524" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg436"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 145.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 141 of the 4th instant,
                    concerning the critical condition of affairs in the island of Ponape, and the
                    efforts of the American missionaries to bring about better relations between the
                    natives and the Spanish Government, I now inclose for your information a copy of
                    a recent letter from the Secretary of the American Board of Commissioners for
                    Foreign Missions and a copy of a despatch from our Minister at Honolulu, both
                    relating to the same subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>









